{"content":[{"c":["PHARAOH’S DAUGHTER"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Egyptian princess who rescued the infant Moses and adopted him as her own son (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.2.5-10","r":"Exod.2.5-10","rawR":"Exod.2.5-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.2.5-10","value":"Exod.2.5-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 2:5-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.7.21","r":"Acts.7.21","rawR":"Acts.7.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.7.21","value":"Acts.7.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 7:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.11.24","r":"Heb.11.24","rawR":"Heb.11.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.11.24","value":"Heb.11.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 11:24"},"). If one accepts an early date for the exodus, this foster mother of Moses could have been Hatshepsut. Some scholars who accept a later date for the exodus believe the pharaoh of the oppression was Ramses II; if so, this princess may have been the daughter of Seti I or the daughter of a pharaoh of the later 18th dynasty. It is likely that she was born to a concubine from a royal harem near the region of Goshen."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. An Egyptian princess, one of the two wives of Mered (a descendant of Caleb) who gave birth to three children (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.17","r":"1Chr.4.17","rawR":"1Chr.4.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.17","value":"1Chr.4.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:17"},"). Her name, Bithiah (meaning “daughter of the ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"divine-name","t":"span"},"”), implies that she was converted to the worship of Israel’s God. It is not known which pharaoh was her father."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Princess whom Solomon married in order to seal an alliance with Egypt. Her father was probably Siamun (978–959 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). He gave to Solomon the town of Gezer as a marriage dowry (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.3.1","r":"1Kgs.3.1","rawR":"1Kgs.3.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.3.1","value":"1Kgs.3.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 3:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.9.16","r":"1Kgs.9.16","rawR":"1Kgs.9.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.9.16","value":"1Kgs.9.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.11.1","r":"1Kgs.11.1","rawR":"1Kgs.11.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.11.1","value":"1Kgs.11.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:1"},"). Solomon built her a palace in Jerusalem because he would not have her live in David’s house (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.7.8","r":"1Kgs.7.8","rawR":"1Kgs.7.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.7.8","value":"1Kgs.7.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 7:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.9.24","r":"1Kgs.9.24","rawR":"1Kgs.9.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.9.24","value":"1Kgs.9.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.8.11","r":"2Chr.8.11","rawR":"2Chr.8.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.8.11","value":"2Chr.8.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 8:11"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"PharaohsDaughter","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 2:5-10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.2.5-10","rawQueryValue":"Exod.2.5-10","sourceRefExact":"Exod.2.5-10"},{"anchorText":"Acts 7:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.7.21","rawQueryValue":"Acts.7.21","sourceRefExact":"Acts.7.21"},{"anchorText":"Heb 11:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Heb.11.24","rawQueryValue":"Heb.11.24","sourceRefExact":"Heb.11.24"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 4:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.4.17","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.4.17","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.4.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 3:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.3.1","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.3.1","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.3.1"},{"anchorText":"9:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.9.16","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.9.16","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.9.16"},{"anchorText":"11:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.11.1","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.11.1","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.11.1"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 7:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.7.8","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.7.8","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.7.8"},{"anchorText":"9:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.9.24","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.9.24","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.9.24"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 8:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.8.11","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.8.11","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.8.11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7480a5db75ce793a0d364244deecf3cce462bddcf3adac15590eaf1532134900","sourceItemName":"PharaohsDaughter","sourceItemOrder":150,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"PharaohsDaughter","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Pharaoh’s Daughter","title":"Pharaoh’s Daughter","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}